  "question": {
    "text": "A car starting from rest accelerates at the rate $f$ through a distance $S$, then continues at constant speed for time $t$ and then decelerates at the rate $f / 2$ to come to rest. If the total distance traversed is $15 \\mathrm{~S}$, then",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "ktSM1",
      "text": "\n$S=f t$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Qn72w",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{S}=1 / 6 \\mathrm{ft}^2$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "vsgAI",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{S}=1 / 2 \\mathrm{ft}^2$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1yhdX",
      "text": "\nNone of these",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/f44uaYu5WyQwBGx5gyyxOdjFgrfaZU9zGiMgi8e5BD0.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\mathrm{S}=\\frac{\\mathrm{ft}_1^2}{2} \\\\\n& \\mathrm{v}_0=\\sqrt{2 \\mathrm{Sf}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nDuring retardation\n$$\nS_2=2 S\n$$\nDuring constant velocity\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& 15 \\mathrm{~S}-3 \\mathrm{~S}=12 \\mathrm{~S}=\\mathrm{v}_0 \\mathrm{t} \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{S}=\\frac{\\mathrm{ft}^2}{72}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
